tyle frames are but I I'm not  a designer  I've never taken in our class I've never  taken a drawing class no type of art  class ever even in high school I would  typically do the more academic based  programs versus like the more fun free  program or the more fun artistic  programs I did some theater and things  like that but I was scared to death  honestly so scared to death I'm like I  know I was just straight-up with them  and that's the thing when you freelance  you need to be honest with people  upfront with people so I just told the  creative director I said hey listen man  like I've never designed stuff frames  before I don't even know how to do this  and he was straight up with me and he  believed me and he said you know what  Cameron he's  I've seen your work I've seen your  animation I've seen how you can post  things you can do this so I put together  my first set of frames I believe is for  Verizon maybe the the cell phone company  and I you know I spent several days on  these frames and I reluctantly handed  them off thinking they're gonna say well  you know they're okay but to my  amazement they loved what I did the  client Verizon actually picked my frames  to move forward with it with and the  next thing I know I'm now a motion  designer a true motion designer I'm I'm  animating I'm also designing and that's  something else we'll talk about in a  future video is that I believe as a  motion designer generalist which many of  us are you need to understand motion as  well as design it's very important that  you understand design as well so from  there it just it took off I just I  continue to freelance I continue to be a  remote artist it was very important to  me to be able to stay in Kansas City  with my kids I had two kids at this  point and just to be a very present  father to them so I continued my remote  freelance career every one small I would  travel to a city to work for a new  production company once they realized my  talent and who I was and I was a  reliable person they would then come  back to me and continue to give me  remote work you know month after month  so I continued to remote freelance I  mean that was in 2007  no one was was doing it at the time or  very few people were doing at the time  and it just took off from there and I  could just continued over the years to  hone my skills to you know just really  improve my skills and that came from me  just working on a variety of types of  projects from projects where I was only  animating our projects where I was only  designing our projects where I was doing  both there was projects where I was in  charge of the overall creativity of a  project and there was projects were only  worked on you know five seconds of a  piece and I was just part of a team it  didn't matter because I just continued  to do what I could do best  that is the moral I guess the moral of  the story is and this is a long story  about my my journey but it's that  anybody can do this if you put in the  time and you put in the effort and you  just you push yourself and you get  uncomfortable and you do things that  scare you  you will become a amazing motion  designer you just have to put in the  time I see a lot of motion designers who  just they want that instant satisfaction  they think that if they learned this  program or this program or this program  that that's the key now you need to  understand motion and design you need to  just dive in the trenches you need to  experiment push yourself creatively and  you will get there and I mean I'm  testament to that I also have other  motion designer friends who have very  similar stories who just kind of came up  from from nowhere and became amazing  artists so you don't have to have the  traditional art school you don't have to  know how to draw you do have to  understand some basic concepts of design  to become an amazing motion designer but  you can do it so hopefully my story will  help you feel inspired to think that you  can and to know that you can do it and  that's all I've got for you today thanks  for taking the time to watch this video  there's gonna be more of these coming  out very soon until next time I'm  Cameron and this is motion science  [Music]
 

